# WN22-MS-000140: Windows Server 2022 must be running Credential Guard on domain-joined member servers.
# Source: Windows Server 2022 STIG r8
# Severity: high
# Generated from 01-extract/output/windows-server-2022-stig-r8-controls.json

META
    esp_id `win2022-wn22-ms-000140-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `windows`
    criticality `critical`

    title `Windows Server 2022 must be running Credential Guard on domain-joined member servers.`
    description `Credential Guard uses virtualization-based security to protect data that could be used in credential theft attacks if compromised. This authentication information, which was stored in the Local Security Authority (LSA) in previous versions of Windows, is isolated from the rest of operating system and can only be accessed by privileged system software.`
    author `scanset-security`
    tags `windows,server-2022,stig,registry,high,ksi-cmt-lmc,ksi-cmt-rmv,ksi-mla-evc,ksi-svc-acm`

    control_mapping `KSI:KSI-CMT-LMC,KSI:KSI-CMT-RMV,KSI:KSI-MLA-EVC,KSI:KSI-SVC-ACM,NIST-800-53:CM-6`
    control_objective `KSI-CMT-LMC,KSI-CMT-RMV,KSI-MLA-EVC,KSI-SVC-ACM`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `Windows:server-2022:endpoint`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `1`
    recommendation `Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration >> Administrative Templates >> System >> Device Guard >> Turn On Virtualization Based Security to "Enabled" with "Enabled with UEFI lock" selected for "Credential Guard Configuration". A Microsoft article on Credential Guard system requirement can be found at the following link: https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/security/identity-protection/credential-guard/credential-guard-requirements Severity Override Guidance: The AO can allow the `

    component_id `comp-windows-registry`

    impl_KSI_CMT_LMC `Windows Server implements KSI-CMT-LMC by setting registry value 'LsaCfgFlags' under 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Windows\DeviceGuard' to the STIG-mandated REG_DWORD value. The ESP scanner reads the value via the registry CTN and fails the policy if the key is absent or the value does not match the required setting. Remediation restores the configuration via Group Policy or direct registry edit per the STIG fix guidance.`
    impl_KSI_CMT_RMV `Windows Server implements KSI-CMT-RMV by setting registry value 'LsaCfgFlags' under 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Windows\DeviceGuard' to the STIG-mandated REG_DWORD value. The ESP scanner reads the value via the registry CTN and fails the policy if the key is absent or the value does not match the required setting. Remediation restores the configuration via Group Policy or direct registry edit per the STIG fix guidance.`
    impl_KSI_MLA_EVC `Windows Server implements KSI-MLA-EVC by setting registry value 'LsaCfgFlags' under 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Windows\DeviceGuard' to the STIG-mandated REG_DWORD value. The ESP scanner reads the value via the registry CTN and fails the policy if the key is absent or the value does not match the required setting. Remediation restores the configuration via Group Policy or direct registry edit per the STIG fix guidance.`
    impl_KSI_SVC_ACM `Windows Server implements KSI-SVC-ACM by setting registry value 'LsaCfgFlags' under 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Windows\DeviceGuard' to the STIG-mandated REG_DWORD value. The ESP scanner reads the value via the registry CTN and fails the policy if the key is absent or the value does not match the required setting. Remediation restores the configuration via Group Policy or direct registry edit per the STIG fix guidance.`
    impl_CM_6 `Windows Server implements CM-6 by setting registry value 'LsaCfgFlags' under 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Windows\DeviceGuard' to the STIG-mandated REG_DWORD value. The ESP scanner reads the value via the registry CTN and fails the policy if the key is absent or the value does not match the required setting. Remediation restores the configuration via Group Policy or direct registry edit per the STIG fix guidance.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT target
        hive `HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE`
        key `SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Windows\DeviceGuard`
        name `LsaCfgFlags`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE compliant
        exists boolean = true
        value_int int = 1
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN registry
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF compliant
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
